{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_80","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' PR_COMMENTS.md\"","aggregated_output":"Implemented 14 new enteric/myenteric neuron classes in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`, covering the requested Dogiel type II, intrinsic primary afferent, myenteric interneuron, secretomotor/vasodilator, intestinofugal, ascending/descending interneuron, stubby/spiny Dogiel type I, calretinin-positive/negative IPAN, and cholinergic/nitrergic grouping terms.\n\nRationale and modeling choices:\n- Added new `CL_99xxxxx` IDs, labels, textual definitions, synonyms, `terms:date`, `terms:creator`, and `IAO:0000233` issue links for all new terms.\n- Used conservative logical axioms that match existing CL practice for neuron location and neurotransmitter groupings, especially `has soma location` in `UBERON:0002439`, plus existing `cholinergic neuron` and `nitrergic neuron` parents for the two grouping classes.\n- Created `dogiel type II neuron of myenteric plexus` as the intersection of the new general `dogiel type II neuron` and the new myenteric intrinsic primary afferent neuron term.\n- Avoided formal use of `CL:0000099` (`interneuron`) for the myenteric interneuron classes after `robot reason` showed that parent makes enteric interneurons unsatisfiable because `CL:0000099` is currently constrained to the central nervous system in this ontology.\n- Did not add projection-target axioms for `intestinofugal neuron` or positive/negative calretinin marker axioms, because the necessary relations/imports are not already modeled cleanly in this file and I avoided speculative ontology additions.\n- `PMID:40954253` from the issue did not resolve during literature checking, so the definitions rely on the other cited references (`PMID:34170401`, `PMID:37355216`, `PMID:32888429`, `PMID:38292899`).\n\nValidation performed:\n- `robot convert -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/cl-edit.owl`\n- `robot reason -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/cl-reasoned.owl`\n\nChecklist:\n- [x] Read the imported issue context\n- [x] Checked existing CL terms and parent consistency in `cl-edit.owl`\n- [x] Reviewed the cited literature that could be accessed\n- [x] Added the requested new terms with definitions and issue tracking annotations\n- [x] Ran syntax/reasoning validation and adjusted the modeling to remove an unsatisfiability\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
